we learned this morning that an  additional 6.6 million people have lost  jobs and filed for unemployment benefits  now the real numbers are actually much  worse than the official numbers and I'll  explain why in a moment  you might remember that two weeks ago we  learned that in the prior week 3.3  million people lost their jobs last week  we learned that the week before 6.8  million people filed for unemployment  and today we learned that last week 6.6  million more people filed for  unemployment benefits that now gets us  to sixteen point seven million people  losing their jobs and filing for  unemployment benefits in just three  weeks now to understand the magnitude of  this the labor force was right around a  hundred and fifty eight million before  this started that means ten percent of  the labor force has filed for  unemployment benefits in the last three  weeks now the question is can we trust  that number well we can trust it but the  real number is much higher why well  number one there are tons of people who  lost a job but don't qualify for  unemployment benefits not every type of  job necessarily qualifies for  unemployment benefits there are people  who are working under the table as the  phrase maybe there are people in certain  jobs where you don't qualify for  unemployment benefits so the real number  is higher and number two the systems for  filing have been so overwhelmed that  there are tons of people who have been  trying to file but couldn't unemployment  is man administered managed at the state  level like we have the department in  Massud the Massachusetts Department of  Employment that manages Massachusetts  unemployment the websites are often not  up to the the task of handling the  increased traffic the phone systems are  often collapsing so there are lots of  people who have been trying to file but  haven't been able to so in early May the  April unemployment report is going to be  released and it could conceivably hit  fifteen percent unemployment which would  be historically high I mean you have to  go back to the Great Depression era  where you had you know 25 percent in  1933 we've not seen numbers like that 15  maybe even we could get to 20% since  these are tragic numbers it's going to  take a long time to recover regardless  of Trump saying it's gonna go up like a  rocket and we're gonna be reinstating  everything very quickly a lot of jobs  are not going to be reinstated as the  economy starts to open back up many  restaurants and other businesses are not  coming back they are closed for good  it's going to be a long process many  people will be starting essentially from  scratch looking for new jobs now a few  reminders here is Donald Trump's press  I'm sorry Commerce Secretary Wilbur Ross  saying just weeks ago that coronavirus  will be good for the economy while  giving us a hacking cough as he says it  take a look I don't want to talk about a  victory lap over a very unfortunate very  malignant disease but the fact is it  does give businesses yet another thing  to consider when they go through their  review of their supply chain on top of  all the other things because that you  had SARS you have the African swine  virus there now you have this  it's another risk factor that people  need to take into account so I think it  will help to accelerate the return of  jobs to North America some to us  probably some to Mexico so we can add  that to the montage of really clueless  people who have no idea what they're  talking about now in the meantime and  we're going to talk about this in the  interview segment today people still  haven't gotten their 1200 dollar  stimulus cheques from reports I'm seeing  the unemployment supplement from the  federal government of up to $600 a week  still hasn't started in many if not  almost all of the states that are  through which people are receiving  unemployment benefits not to a  significant degree  despite Trump's claims during his press  conferences that billions and billions  of dollars in the Paycheck Protection  Plan funds have been doled out already  it seems that very few businesses have  actually received any money so far we're  months into this thing now and where are  those benefits where is the money these  are very  numbers they are made worse by the fact  that the Trump administration has been  so brutally behind on all of this so we  need a government that can actually  behave responsibly and react quickly we  don't have it right now there's a  YouTube channel we're partnering with  that I would love for you to check out  it's a channel called up flip you can  get there by clicking the link below  make sure you subscribe when you're  there every week up flip uploads a new  video where you get an exclusive  behind-the-scenes look at a different  small business everything from real  estate firms coffee shops auto repair  shops each business owner shares a ton  of really interesting insight about how  they built their business what it's like  day-to-day how they got to where they  are fascinating to learn about other  people's business strategies how they  found success it's a great channel for  anyone thinking of starting a business  already running one or just people  interested in how different business  work perfect for people who like TV  shows like shark tank and that type of  thing check it out at david pakman.com  slash up flip the link is underneath the  video they are friends of the David  Pakman show make sure to subscribe when  you're there click that Bell icon to be  notified when they upload new videos
 

